From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: rdoupe <1207041+rdoupe@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 20 Oct 2026 00:00:00 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] gpiolib: acpi: Add a quirk for ASUS ROG Zephyrus G16 GA605KM

With an external monitor connected (HDMI, driven by the dGPU), the
ASUS ROG Zephyrus G16 GA605KM wakes about 95 ms after entering s2idle,
on battery and on AC. The wakeup comes from the _AEI event on GPIO 16
of AMDI0030:00: "ACPI: PM: Wakeup unrelated to ACPI SCI", "GPIO 16 is
active". Without a monitor the same machine sleeps normally.

Booting with gpiolib_acpi.ignore_wake=AMDI0030:00@16 fixes it: with
HDMI connected the machine reaches hardware sleep for 10-44 s per
cycle, and the lid (GPIO 0) and the keyboard still wake it. Add the
same as a DMI quirk, like the existing ignore_wake entries.

Tested on BIOS GA605KM.307.

Downstream carry for omarchy-asus (G16 GA605 repo). Not yet submitted
upstream (linux-gpio); drop it once an equivalent entry is merged.

Assisted-by: LLM
---
 drivers/gpio/gpiolib-acpi-quirks.c | 15 +++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 15 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/gpio/gpiolib-acpi-quirks.c b/drivers/gpio/gpiolib-acpi-quirks.c
--- a/drivers/gpio/gpiolib-acpi-quirks.c
+++ b/drivers/gpio/gpiolib-acpi-quirks.c
@@ -419,6 +419,21 @@
 			.ignore_irq_active_low = "INTC10BC:01@20",
 		},
 	},
+	{
+		/*
+		 * Spurious wakeups from the _AEI GPIO 16 when an external monitor is
+		 * connected (HDMI, driven by the dGPU): the system wakes ~95 ms after
+		 * entering s2idle. Lid (GPIO 0) and keyboard wakeups are unaffected.
+		 * ASUS ROG Zephyrus G16 GA605KM, BIOS GA605KM.307.
+		 */
+		.matches = {
+			DMI_MATCH(DMI_SYS_VENDOR, "ASUSTeK COMPUTER INC."),
+			DMI_MATCH(DMI_BOARD_NAME, "GA605KM"),
+		},
+		.driver_data = &(struct acpi_gpiolib_dmi_quirk) {
+			.ignore_wake = "AMDI0030:00@16",
+		},
+	},
 	{} /* Terminating entry */
 };
 
